  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 901 PM CDT Sun Sep 13 2026\n\nThe TN Valley won't find a break from the heat in the Long Term. \nThe lingering ridge across the Southeast will start to retrograde \nas a cut off low pushes into FL starting on Thursday. With a sfc \nhigh anchored across the east coast, highs will remain in the 90s \nthrough the week. However, the low will pull additional moisture \ninto the region, pushing Heat Index values around 100 degrees, but\nat this time below any advisory criteria. The low will slide \nwestward across the northern Gulf through the weekend, and this \nwill allow for a front in the Ozarks and OH Valley to dip \nsouthward towards the TN Valley. Models still disagree on if the \nfront will make it in or not this weekend and the outcome will \nhave an effect on our temps, cloud cover, and our precip chances. \nIf it moves through, we could have a quick break in the heat but \nincreased rain chances, but if it remains to our north, hot and \nhumid conditions will persist. Will stick with guidance that has \nthe 90s lingering, heat index values still hovering around 100 \ndegrees and low precip chances (15-25% Sat, 20-30% Sunday). \nHowever, trends will be monitored for future needed adjustments.",
